    "description": "Antique Southwestern silver belt components featuring two large hand hammered open center fittings and two decorative bowtie spacers with stamped and repousse style detailing. The bowtie pieces are characteristic of spacers used on early concho belts, while the larger pieces retain leather remnants and hand formed attachment hardware. Navajo or Southwestern attribution is plausible, but no maker or tribal marks are present.\nThe bowtie pieces tested 94.8% silver by XRF and weigh appr. 13.53g combined. The larger pieces tested 92.8% silver and weigh appr. 42.00g combined. Variations in silver purity are compatible with older hand worked Southwestern silver. See photos for measurements and condition details.",
